<div id="android-mdm" v-cloak>
  <div purpose="landing-page-container">
    <div purpose="landing-page-content">
      <div purpose="landing-page-hero">
        <div purpose="hero-row">
          <div purpose="page-hero-content">
            <div purpose="page-hero-headings">
              <h4>Android Device Management</h4>
              <h1>AI-native Android MDM for modern IT and security teams</h1>
            </div>
            <div purpose="page-hero-text">
              <p>Enroll, configure, and secure Android phones and tablets at enterprise scale. Say what you need done, approve the change, and Fleet handles the rest. Manage Android alongside macOS, iOS, iPadOS, Windows, Linux, and ChromeOS in one place.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="button-row">
              <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <a purpose="hero-quote" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/luismadrigal/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" no-icon>
            <div purpose="hero-quote-profile-image">
              <img alt="Luis Madrigal, former engineering leader at Uber" src="/images/testimonial-author-luis-madrigal-100x100@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="quote-author-info">
              <p purpose="quote-text">“Fleet aligns with the strategies that enabled me to help scale Uber’s global device deployments with a lean DevOps/systems engineering team.”</p>
              <p purpose="quote-author-name">Luis Madrigal</p>
              <p purpose="quote-author-title">Former Engineering Leader, Uber</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div purpose="hero-logos">
          <logo-carousel></logo-carousel>
        </div>
      </div><%/* landing-page-hero */%>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h3>Traditional Android MDM is holding IT back</h3>
          <p>Most Android management tools bolt onto a closed-source console with limited support for modern Android Enterprise, weak BYOD privacy, and no real cross-platform story.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="four-column-feature-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Vendor lock-in</h5>
            <p>Proprietary tools trap configurations behind GUIs, with steep renewals and limited export.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Slow, risky changes</h5>
            <p>Profile and policy changes happen by hand in a console, with no review and no history.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Android afterthought</h5>
            <p>Tools designed around Windows or Mac treat Android as a checkbox, not a first-class platform.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>BYOD privacy concerns</h5>
            <p>Legacy agents reach into personal data on employee-owned phones, eroding trust and adoption.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="feature-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <h3>Get AI working for you</h3>
            <p>Fleet works natively with your team’s AI tools, like Claude, Copilot, or any AI harness. Say what you need done. AI proposes the change, and a person on your team approves it before it touches a device. Practice it live at a <a href="/workshops">free workshop</a> and get certified.</p>
            <div purpose="checklist">
              <p>Draft Android configuration profiles and managed app configurations from a plain-language prompt.</p>
              <p>Ask questions about your devices in plain language.</p>
              <p>Review every change before it ships, and undo any mistake.</p>
              <p>Change Android, <a href="/apple">Apple</a>, and <a href="/windows">Windows</a> settings together, in one request.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-image">
            <img alt="A screenshot of Fleet running reports across managed devices." src="/images/linux-management-feature-image-scripts-504x378@2x.png">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="feature-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-image">
            <img alt="A screenshot of Fleet managing Android devices." src="/images/fleet-mdm-hero-1006x595@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <h3>Manage Android with the visibility and control modern IT teams need</h3>
            <p>Fleet is AI-native Android device management built on Google's Android Management API and Android Enterprise. Enroll, configure, and secure every Android device, BYOD or company-owned, without giving up transparency or cross-platform support.</p>
            <div purpose="checklist">
              <p>Connect Android Enterprise to Fleet with a free subscription through Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, or any work email.</p>
              <p>Enroll personal Android hosts with a Work Profile that keeps personal data separate from corporate apps.</p>
              <p>Enroll company-owned Android hosts in fully-managed mode for stricter controls beyond what a Work Profile allows, or automatically on first boot with <a href="/guides/android-zero-touch-enrollment">Android zero-touch</a>.</p>
              <p>Push configuration profiles, managed app configurations, and certificates, with a person reviewing every change before it ships.</p>
              <p>Deploy public and private Android apps from managed Google Play, including custom APKs.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Corporate phones and rugged devices</h2>
          <p>Android shows up at work in two very different ways. Fleet manages both, from the same console as your <a href="/apple">Macs</a>, <a href="/windows">PCs</a>, and <a href="/linux">Linux</a> devices.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Corporate Android</h5>
            <p>Phones and tablets for knowledge workers, either company-owned or personal. Personal phones get a Work Profile, so work apps and data stay separate from everything else. Company phones are fully managed. Either way, employees install the apps they need from self-service, and IT gets the same live reporting it has for laptops.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Rugged Android</h5>
            <p>Purpose-built handhelds and tablets for warehouses, loading docks, store floors, and drivers on the road. They’re often shared, run a few line-of-business apps, and stay in the field for years, so you support several Android versions at once. Fleet enrolls them as fully managed devices with <a href="/guides/android-zero-touch-enrollment">Android zero-touch</a>, delivers private apps and app configurations through managed Google Play, and pushes Wi-Fi certificates, without anyone in IT touching the device.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Built for Android Enterprise</h2>
          <p>Whether you manage a handful of field devices or tens of thousands of phones, Fleet gives Android admins the depth Google's platform deserves and the cross-platform reach the rest of the business needs.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Android Enterprise integration</h5>
            <p>Connect Android Enterprise to Fleet in minutes. Free subscription, no extra cost from Google to manage your hosts.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>BYOD Work Profile</h5>
            <p>Enroll personal Android devices with a Work Profile that segments corporate apps and data from the user's personal information.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Fully-managed company devices</h5>
            <p>Enroll company-owned Android hosts in fully-managed mode for stricter controls and management features not available on BYOD.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>QR code and link enrollment</h5>
            <p>Send end users a Fleet enrollment link or QR code. The Work Profile sets up in a few taps.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Configuration profiles</h5>
            <p>Apply policies and settings with configuration profiles, from password complexity to network configuration. Describe the setting you want, and AI drafts the profile for your review.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Managed Google Play apps</h5>
            <p>Add free public apps from Google Play and deploy them to fleets or via self-service. Apps install silently in the Work Profile.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Custom Android apps (APK)</h5>
            <p>Publish private APKs through managed Google Play and deliver them to your hosts. Updates flow the same way.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Managed app configurations</h5>
            <p>Configure app behavior centrally with managed app configurations, so apps land pre-configured for your environment.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Enterprise Wi-Fi with EAP-TLS</h5>
            <p>Deploy SCEP certificates and 802.1X EAP-TLS Wi-Fi configurations to fully-managed and Work Profile hosts. Fleet auto-renews certificates 30 days before expiration.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Self-service software</h5>
            <p>Publish apps to a per-user managed Google Play self-service catalog. End users install what they need without filing a ticket.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>BYOD migration from another MDM</h5>
            <p>Move users to Fleet with a single enrollment link. End users remove the old Work Profile in device settings, then enroll in Fleet, no full device wipe required.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Self-hosted or Fleet-hosted, your data, your jurisdiction</h2>
          <p>Run Fleet on your own infrastructure or on Fleet Cloud, with the same features either way. Device data lives where your security and compliance teams decide, not where a vendor's multi-tenant cloud puts it.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Open source core</h5>
            <p>Fleet is MIT-licensed open source. Read the code, audit how Android hosts are managed, and adapt it to your needs. No major Android MDM offers this.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Run it where you want</h5>
            <p>Deploy Fleet on AWS, Azure, GCP, or your own data center, or use Fleet Cloud with 100% feature parity. Android MDM requires outbound access to Google for Pub/Sub notifications.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>One console, every platform</h5>
            <p>See Android, <a href="/apple">macOS, iOS, iPadOS</a>, <a href="/windows">Windows</a>, <a href="/linux">Linux</a>, and ChromeOS in one inventory and one policy engine. No separate Android MDM, no separate Linux tool.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>API-first by design</h5>
            <p>Every feature in the Fleet UI is available over the REST API. Integrate with Okta, Jira, Slack, Snowflake, and your SIEM.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Play Protect certified hosts</h5>
            <p>Fleet supports Android devices that are Play Protect certified, including Google Pixel and Samsung Galaxy.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Built in the open</h5>
            <p>Fleet's roadmap, code, and conversations are public. File an issue, send a PR, or ship a feature with us.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Android MDM frequently asked questions</h2>
        </div>
        <div purpose="faq" class="d-flex flex-column">
          <div purpose="accordion" class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-start">
            <div purpose="accordion-body">
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="android-faq__header1" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#android-faq__body1" aria-controls="android-faq__body1">
                  What do I need to turn on Android MDM in Fleet?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="android-faq__body1" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="android-faq__header1">
                  An Android Enterprise subscription, which is free. Connect it to Fleet through Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, or any work email. To learn more, check out the <a href="/guides/android-mdm-setup">Android MDM setup guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="android-faq__header2" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#android-faq__body2" aria-controls="android-faq__body2">
                  Can employees enroll personal Android phones?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="android-faq__body2" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="android-faq__header2">
                  Yes. Personal Android devices enroll with a Work Profile that keeps corporate apps and data separate from the user’s personal information. End users enroll with a Fleet enrollment link or QR code.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="android-faq__header3" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#android-faq__body3" aria-controls="android-faq__body3">
                  Can company-owned Android devices enroll automatically?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="android-faq__body3" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="android-faq__header3">
                  Yes. Connect Fleet to the Android zero-touch portal so company-owned devices enroll automatically on first boot. Devices must be purchased from an authorized zero-touch reseller. To learn more, check out the <a href="/guides/android-zero-touch-enrollment">Android zero-touch enrollment guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="android-faq__header4" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#android-faq__body4" aria-controls="android-faq__body4">
                  Can Fleet manage rugged Android devices?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="android-faq__body4" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="android-faq__header4">
                  Yes. Fleet manages rugged Android handhelds and tablets, like the scanners used in warehouses and on loading docks, as fully managed company devices. Enroll them automatically with <a href="/guides/android-zero-touch-enrollment">Android zero-touch</a>, deliver line-of-business apps and managed app configurations through managed Google Play, and push Wi-Fi certificates. Devices need Google Play services. <a href="/contact?talkToUs">Talk to us</a> about the rugged hardware you run.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="android-faq__header5" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#android-faq__body5" aria-controls="android-faq__body5">
                  Can I migrate Android devices from another MDM without a wipe?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="android-faq__body5" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="android-faq__header5">
                  Yes, for personal devices. End users remove the old Work Profile in device settings, then enroll in Fleet with a single link. No full device wipe is required. To learn more, check out the <a href="/guides/android-byod-mdm-migration">Android BYOD migration guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="android-faq__header6" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#android-faq__body6" aria-controls="android-faq__body6">
                  How do I deploy apps to Android devices?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="android-faq__body6" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="android-faq__header6">
                  Add free public apps from managed Google Play, or publish private APKs through managed Google Play. Deploy them to your devices or offer them in self-service. To learn more, check out the guide to <a href="/guides/deploy-custom-android-app-apk">deploying custom Android apps</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="android-faq__header7" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#android-faq__body7" aria-controls="android-faq__body7">
                  Which Android devices does Fleet support?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="android-faq__body7" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="android-faq__header7">
                  Fleet supports Android devices that are Play Protect certified, including Google Pixel and Samsung Galaxy.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="android-faq__header8" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#android-faq__body8" aria-controls="android-faq__body8">
                  Can Fleet manage Android alongside Apple and Windows?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="android-faq__body8" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="android-faq__header8">
                  Yes. Fleet manages Android, <a href="/apple">macOS, iOS, and iPadOS</a>, <a href="/windows">Windows</a>, <a href="/linux">Linux</a>, and ChromeOS from one console, with the same API and the same AI-native workflow.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="android-faq__header9" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#android-faq__body9" aria-controls="android-faq__body9">
                  Does Android MDM work if I self-host Fleet?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="android-faq__body9" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="android-faq__header9">
                  Yes. Android MDM needs a network connection between your Fleet server and Google, which Fleet uses for Pub/Sub notifications. To learn more, check out <a href="/guides/how-fleets-android-mdm-connects-to-google">how Fleet’s Android MDM connects to Google</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="d-flex flex-row justify-content-start">
              <p purpose="contact-note">Have another question? <a href="/docs/get-started/faq">Read the full FAQ</a> or <a href="/contact">talk to an engineer</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
